 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Hotel Booking Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a hotel booking form?\", \"a\": \"A hotel booking form is how a guest asks a property for a room. It collects the dates, the room type, the number of guests, and a way to pay or hold the room. Online, it can check those dates against the rooms left before anything reaches the front desk.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a hotel booking form?\", \"a\": \"Write down the rooms you sell and the rules for each night first: minimum stays, deposits, group cutoffs. Describe them to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> in plain English. Emergent builds the form with the room table behind it, and you change either one by asking.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free hotel booking form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Each tab on this page works as a free hotel booking form template: open the prompt behind the one closest to your property and swap in your room count and rates. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing the form.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a hotel booking form template include?\", \"a\": \"Every template needs the stay dates and the room type, plus the party size and a way to reach the guest. Small properties often add an arrival time and a box for special requests. Show the total for the stay and the deposit due before the guest presses submit.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a room booking form and a hotel booking form?\", \"a\": \"The difference is scope. A room booking form asks for one room on set dates, and offices use the same name for meeting rooms booked by the hour. A hotel booking form covers the whole stay, with several rooms, the guests in each, and any group rate. For hourly rentals, a general <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/booking-form'>booking form</a> fits better.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is an online hotel booking form better than a paper one?\", \"a\": \"For most properties, yes. A hotel booking form PDF suits attendees who prefer to fill in a sheet and email it back. Each returned sheet then has to be typed in by hand and checked against the rooms already sold, while an online form writes each request straight to a table. Planners can pair the online form with a conference registration form for the sign-ups.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I customize a hotel booking form template?\", \"a\": \"Replace the sample rooms and rates with your own, then add the rules your property runs on, such as a two-night weekend minimum. In a document template, that means editing the file by hand every season. With Emergent, you describe the change in plain English, and the form and its room table update together.\"}, {\"q\": \"What format should a hotel booking form follow?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to one screen, with the stay dates first, since every later answer depends on them. Cancellation terms belong right above the submit button, not in a footer. On a phone, the dates should open a calendar, and the room list should show only rooms open for every night chosen.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a free hotel booking form enough for a small hotel?\", \"a\": \"It can be for a handful of rooms. A free form that collects names and dates leaves the desk to compare each request with the calendar and reply by hand. Once a two-night weekend minimum or a deposit comes into play, the form needs to check those rules before the guest can send it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a hotel booking form send the guest after they submit?\", \"a\": \"A confirmation that repeats the stay and the total, with the deposit paid and the balance still due. Add the cancellation terms and the check-in time, along with anything the desk checks on arrival, such as photo ID in the booking name. A request still waiting on approval should say when the guest will hear back.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}